## Request Payload Structure

Every inbound webhook from the treasury system arrives as an HTTP `POST` with the following shape.

### Headers

| Header | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `X-Treasury-Signature` | `string` | HMAC-SHA256 of the raw request body, hex-encoded |
| `X-Treasury-Timestamp` | `string` | Unix timestamp (seconds) when the event was generated |
| `X-Treasury-Event-ID` | `string` | Globally unique event identifier (UUID v4) |
| `Content-Type` | `string` | Always `application/json` |

### Body Schema

```json
{
  "event_id": "f3a1c2d4-89ab-4cde-b012-3456789abcde",
  "event_type": "payment.completed",
  "timestamp": 1718300000,
  "version": "2.1",
  "payment": {
    "payment_id": "PAY-2024-00847362",
